  "details": "Currently, creating a Group Instance in VRChat requires selecting the region twice, which can be confusing and redundant.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Open VRChat.\n\n2. Open the Large Menu.\n\n3. Select a World.\n\n4. Click \"Create New Instance.\"\n\n5. Select \"Group.\"\n\n6. Choose a region (for example, USE).\n\n7. Select the Group.\n\n8. Select the Group Instance Type.\n\n9. Select Roles.\n\n10. Scroll down and notice that the region has reverted to the default (USW), even though USE was selected earlier.\n\nThis creates a risk of accidentally creating an instance in the wrong region if the user does not scroll down and verify the setting.\n\nRequest:\n\nPlease make the region selection a single-step process that persists throughout instance creation. Once a region is selected, it should remain unchanged and not require users to verify or select it again later in the workflow.",
